## 4. Direct data points and quotes a strategist can use verbatim

1. **On the operating model:** "Helsinki Airport has been a silent airport since 2015. No flight or passenger announcements are made in the terminal, though announcements in the gate areas as well as emergency announcements are not affected." [Source: https://airport.nridigital.com/air_mar18/shhhh_is_the_day_of_the_airport_announcer_over]

2. **On London City's carve-outs:** "London City Airport maintains a strict 'Silent Airport' policy, with announcements made only for bad weather delays or genuine emergencies." [Source: https://www.londoncityairport.com/silent-airport-policy]

3. **On the intelligibility floor MWAA should specify:** ACRP Research Report 175 recommends STI ≥ 0.45 and a 10–15 dB(A) signal-to-noise ratio for pier-style departure lounges, and identifies reverberation time below 1.9 seconds as the strongest lever on intelligibility [Source: https://www.wilsonihrig.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/12/ACRP-Report-No.-175_Wilson-Ihrig.pdf].

4. **On the survey base underlying the reverberation finding:** "Most industry survey respondents (69%) judged high reverberation to be one of the most important factors hindering passengers' ability to understand PA announcements." [Source: same ACRP 175 summary]

5. **On the emergency-communication constraint that overrides any quiet policy:** NFPA 72 Chapter 24 requires emergency voice-messaging intelligibility at STI ≥ 0.45 (CIS "Fair"), with best-practice designs targeting STI 0.70 in 90% of the covered area and treating STI 0.50 as an absolute floor [Source: https://www.commercialintegrator.com/security/mass_notification/mass-notification-intelligibility/].

6. **On the operating context at IAD:** IAD served 29,008,839 passengers in 2025 — an all-time record, 6.4% year-over-year growth — with November 2025 on-time performance of 77.38% [Source: https://www.americanairportguide.com/iad/airport-statistics.htm]. The $20B+ decade-long Dulles transformation announced July 29, 2026 is the design window in which mandatory acoustic and PA specifications can be written into program briefs at 30% design cost, not commissioned into completed rooms at 90%.

7. **On the operating context at DCA:** DCA served ~24.9M passengers in 2025 (down 5.3%), absorbed the January 29, 2025 mid-air collision fatalities and its regulatory aftermath, and now operates under permanent FAA helicopter restrictions effective January 23, 2026 [Source: https://simpleflying.com/faa-makes-dc-helicopter-ban-permanent-new-flight-rules-explained/]. This is the brownfield DCA is asking a common MWAA standard to be applied to.

